import{_t as e,it as t,n,rt as r}from"./chunks/framework.B5d4da8a.js";var i=JSON.parse(`{"title":"Retro — conv_channel_scale anchor landed; the fold mints by ITERATED composition","description":"","frontmatter":{},"headers":[],"relativePath":"graphopt/project/retros/conv-channel-scale-anchor.md","filePath":"vendored/graphopt/project/retros/conv-channel-scale-anchor.md"}`),a={name:`graphopt/project/retros/conv-channel-scale-anchor.md`};function o(n,i,a,o,s,c){return e(),r(`div`,null,[...i[0]||=[t(`<h1 id="retro-—-conv-channel-scale-anchor-landed-the-fold-mints-by-iterated-composition" tabindex="-1">Retro — <code>conv_channel_scale</code> anchor landed; the fold mints by ITERATED composition <a class="header-anchor" href="#retro-—-conv-channel-scale-anchor-landed-the-fold-mints-by-iterated-composition" aria-label="Permalink to “Retro — conv_channel_scale anchor landed; the fold mints by ITERATED composition”">​</a></h1><p><strong>Date</strong>: 2026-10-19. <strong>Follows</strong>: <code>conv-bn-fold-synth.md</code> (named the missing <code>conv2d</code>-headed anchor, gate A). <strong>Commit</strong>: <code>945733f</code> (<code>CONV_FOLD_RULES</code> in <code>mlopt_core.laws.tensor</code>, opt-in with <code>BATCH_NORM_RULES</code>). <strong>Probe</strong>: <code>lab/probes/conv_bn_fold_synth_probe.py</code> — re-run, gates A/B/B3/C/D.</p><h2 id="the-anchor-—-conv-fold-rules-60-rules-all-data" tabindex="-1">The anchor — <code>CONV_FOLD_RULES</code> (60 rules, all data) <a class="header-anchor" href="#the-anchor-—-conv-fold-rules-60-rules-all-data" aria-label="Permalink to “The anchor — CONV_FOLD_RULES (60 rules, all data)”">​</a></h2><p>The conv twin of <code>linear_channel_scale</code>, plus its shift sibling — the absorb half of the conv+BN weight-space pair:</p><div class="language-"><button title="Copy code" data-copied="Copied" class="copy"></button><span class="lang"></span><pre class="shiki shiki-themes handl-dark github-light" style="--shiki-dark:#ffffff;--shiki-light:#24292e;--shiki-dark-bg:#2a2a2a;--shiki-light-bg:#fff;" tabindex="0" dir="ltr"><code><span class="line"><span>conv2d(x, W, b) · ŝ  =  conv2d(x, W∘ŝ′, b∘s)      ŝ ~ (1, C, 1, 1)</span></span>
<span class="line"><span>conv2d(x, W, b) ± ĉ  =  conv2d(x, W, b ± c)       ĉ ~ (1, C, 1, 1)</span></span></code></pre></div><ul><li>Per-output-channel scale folds through W&#39;s axis 0 AND the bias; the per-channel shift folds into the bias outright (conv is linear in its filter). <code>linear</code>&#39;s channel scale folds the weight&#39;s INPUT axis — conv&#39;s folds the OUTPUT axis.</li><li>The <code>sv</code>/<code>cv</code> metavar binds <strong>any term whose shape is the channel view</strong> — the fold site carries compounds (<code>γ̂·r̂</code>, <code>ŝ·(−μ̂)+β̂</code>), never a lone reshape. The <code>(C,1,1,1)</code> weight view <code>WV</code> and <code>(C,)</code> bias vector <code>SV</code> are dspec-derived reshapes.</li><li>Guards (data): batched rank-4 conv2d only; <code>x</code>/<code>W</code>/<code>sv</code> concrete; <code>sv == (1, W[0], 1, 1)</code>; <code>F.conv2d</code> well-typedness <code>x[1] == W[1]·G</code> (<code>dim-eq</code> when the export elides <code>groups</code>, <code>attr-cmp</code>×<code>mul</code> when spelled).</li><li><strong>Generated</strong> per (attr-prefix × bias-arity × operand-order × direction): conv2d&#39;s positional tail is a prefix of <code>(stride, padding, dilation, groups)</code> and <code>match_pattern</code> requires an exact attr-key set — 6 shapes × 5 prefixes × 2 arities, the <code>_make_sdpa_fold_rules</code>/<code>SPLIT_SCALAR_RULES</code> precedent.</li><li>Verified fp64 against <code>F.conv2d</code> incl. <code>groups=2</code> (<code>tests/test_conv_fold_rules.py</code>, 10 tests). Opt-in <code>CONV_FOLD_RULES</code> — held out of <code>ALL_RULES</code>/<code>DEFAULT</code> with the BN family pending the admission floor.</li></ul><h2 id="probe-re-run-—-the-measured-account" tabindex="-1">Probe re-run — the measured account <a class="header-anchor" href="#probe-re-run-—-the-measured-account" aria-label="Permalink to “Probe re-run — the measured account”">​</a></h2><p><strong>Gate A — corpus gap closed.</strong> conv2d: 0 → 60 lhs + 60 rhs entries. <strong>Gate B — pairwise <code>synthesize_rules</code> still refuses the bare fold</strong>: <code>rhs_heads_conv2d</code> is False in every bank (DEFAULT+BN, ALL+BN, ALL+BN+CONV, ALL+BN+CONV+PW), <code>fold_composites</code> empty. But the anchor participates immediately: <code>syn_batch_norm_expand__ conv_channel_shift_sub_sp_6</code> mints <code>batch_norm(conv2d(…)) → add(mul(γ̂, mul(conv2d(x,W,b−μ̂), r̂)), β̂)</code> — the running mean absorbed into the conv bias in ONE pairwise composite.</p><p><strong>Gate B3 — iterated composition mints it.</strong> <code>synthesize_rules</code> composes pairs over a FIXED <code>usable</code> list (derivation depth exactly 2; emitted composites never re-enter the pool). Feeding each round&#39;s emitted set into the next round&#39;s bank — <code>usable = base + emitted</code> — the fold mints in <strong>4 rounds</strong> (emitted 26 → 61 → 242 → 944 on fuel=30000):</p><div class="language-"><button title="Copy code" data-copied="Copied" class="copy"></button><span class="lang"></span><pre class="shiki shiki-themes handl-dark github-light" style="--shiki-dark:#ffffff;--shiki-light:#24292e;--shiki-dark-bg:#2a2a2a;--shiki-light-bg:#fff;" tabindex="0" dir="ltr"><code><span class="line"><span>syn_…_batch_norm_expand__conv_channel_shift_sub_sp_6</span></span>
<span class="line"><span>    __conv_channel_scale_sp_48__conv_channel_scale_l_sp_209</span></span>
<span class="line"><span>    __conv_channel_shift_sp_896</span></span></code></pre></div><p>i.e. <code>batch_norm(conv2d(x,W,b),γ,β,μ,σ²) → conv2d(x, W′, b′)</code> — the chain expand → shift_sub → scale → scale_l → shift. Verified <strong>fp64-exact</strong> on the real seed: max diff 6.8e-13 vs the fused kernel (env bound from <code>source_tensors</code> — the <code>randn</code> env NaNs on <code>rv&lt;0</code>, gate B2). W′ spells <code>W·rsqrt(σ²+ε)·γ</code> and b′ <code>(b−μ̂)·ŝ·γ̂ + β̂</code> through the derived <code>CH</code>/<code>WV</code>/<code>SV</code> views.</p><p><strong>Gates C/D unchanged</strong> — <code>dspec_synth</code> mints the derives staged (<code>scale</code>/<code>b′</code> depth 3, <code>W′</code> depth 2 given <code>scale</code>); the one-shot tensor-tier <code>W′</code> still refuses on depth ≥4 + <code>(C,)×(C,i,k,k)</code> broadcast.</p><h2 id="what-stays-open-named-ordered" tabindex="-1">What stays open (named, ordered) <a class="header-anchor" href="#what-stays-open-named-ordered" aria-label="Permalink to “What stays open (named, ordered)”">​</a></h2><ol><li><strong>Composition depth is the refusal, not material.</strong> A <code>synthesize_rules</code> fixpoint knob — feed emitted composites back into <code>usable</code> until convergence or a round cap (the probe&#39;s gate-B3 loop is the reference; a <code>rounds=</code> parameter or a driver in <code>mlopt_discovery</code>) — or the ADR-0008 anchored mint (antiunify over a measured seed↔folded pair) which jumps the depth directly.</li><li><strong>The emitted fold&#39;s guard content.</strong> The minted composite carries the transported conjunction of all five parents&#39; conds; whether it serializes clean through <code>law_to_data</code>/<code>rulecache</code> and what its derived-attr placeholder chain looks like at admission time is unmeasured.</li><li><code>CONV_FOLD_RULES</code> <code>DEFAULT</code>/<code>ALL_RULES</code> admission — the guarded sweep (<code>bn-admission-sweep.md</code> posture), now that the fold actually composes on a real seed.</li><li>Staged <code>dspec_synth</code> + a channel-broadcast <code>mul</code>/<code>tapp</code> in the enumeration bank — the gate-D sub-gaps, unchanged.</li></ol><h2 id="caveats-measured" tabindex="-1">Caveats measured <a class="header-anchor" href="#caveats-measured" aria-label="Permalink to “Caveats measured”">​</a></h2><ul><li><code>numeric_check=True</code> still drops the BN composites — the <code>_tensor_env</code> <code>rv&lt;0</code> → <code>rsqrt</code> NaN artifact (gate B2); the iterated gate runs <code>numeric_check=False</code> and verifies the fold separately on the real tensors.</li><li>The <code>_spdg</code> <code>groups</code> attr-cmp reads <code>x[1] == W[1]·GR</code> — the only clause in the family that multiplies a bound attr; a non-int <code>GR</code> declines (tensor-tier <code>_tcall</code> wraps the error).</li></ul>`,16)]])}var s=n(a,[[`render`,o]]);export{i as __pageData,s as default};